# 3. DESIGN SYSTEM — STRICTLY FOLLOW

Implement the provided Neo-Brutalist design direction throughout the application.

### Color Palette

Primary Yellow: #ffe17c

Deep Charcoal: #171e19

Sage Accent: #b7c6c2

White: #ffffff

Black: #000000

Additional neutral colors may be used for secondary information, disabled states, and error indicators.

### Typography

Headings:
Cabinet Grotesk — weights 400–800.

Body:
Satoshi — Medium 500.

Use bold geometric typography, strong hierarchy, and high readability.

Import both fonts using Google Fonts if available.

### Borders

- All interactive elements must have 2px solid black borders.
- Cards must use 2px borders.
- Sections should use strong visual separation.
- Avoid unnecessary decorative effects.

### Hard Shadows

Standard:
box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px 0px #000000;

Large:
box-shadow: 8px 8px 0px 0px #000000;

Dashboard containers:
box-shadow: 12px 12px 0px 0px #000000;

IMPORTANT:
- Never use blurred shadows.
- Never use gradients.
- Maintain a consistent Neo-Brutalist aesthetic.

### Button Interactions

Buttons should behave like physical push buttons.

Hover:
transform: translate(4px, 4px);

Active:
transform: translate(4px, 4px);

Remove the hard shadow when pressed.

Use smooth transitions.

### Border Radius

- Buttons: Maximum 12px.
- Dashboard cards: 8px–16px.
- Marketing cards: Can use larger asymmetric corners.
- Avoid excessive rounded UI.

